                <pb facs="0424" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.112/15: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Chefoo</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Roberts</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chefoo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-27T09:00:00+08:00">July 27, 1938—9 a.m. [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">p.m.</hi>]</date><lb/>[Received July 27—10:40
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At 3 p.m. today it was reported to me that two Americans, Harry E. Clark and
                    Albert R. Wilkins, were struck by Japanese guard 11:30 p.m., July 26th after
                    curfew. Incident has been reported to Japanese Consul and commander of Japanese
                    landing party has investigated and found Japanese patrol acted without
                    provocation. I am of opinion incident can be settled locally by accepting
                    expression of regret from Japanese commander, punishment of Japanese guards
                    involved and assurance that orders have been issued to prevent similar
                    occurrences. Please send instructions.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Embassy at Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roberts</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
